"answer": "According to the provided sources, normal development for children aged 1-3 includes the following areas: Gross motor (walking, running, climbing), Fine motor (feeding themselves, drawing), Sensory (seeing, hearing, tasting, touching, and smelling), Language (saying single words, then sentences), and Social (playing with others, taking turns, doing fantasy play) [MLP-5424]."
